WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.835
In this lesson, you will learn to use forever loops with if-then conditions to keep checking the world, and build bouncing and wrap-around motion.

2
00:00:12.435 --> 00:00:15.409
A forever loop never stops.

3
00:00:15.409 --> 00:00:21.861
Games, animations and apps run in a loop that keeps checking what’s happening.

4
00:00:22.461 --> 00:00:29.783
If-then means selection: the computer only runs the inside blocks when the condition is true.

5
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:38.574
In many classic games, things that leave one side of the screen come back on the other.

6
00:00:38.574 --> 00:00:42.417
That’s a forever loop with a condition.

7
00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:49.470
Every game runs a game loop: read input, update positions, check collisions, draw.

8
00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:53.748
Forever + if is the heart of it.

9
00:00:54.348 --> 00:01:02.104
In Python, “while True” is a forever loop, and “if” works just like the Scratch block.

10
00:01:02.704 --> 00:01:06.548
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

11
00:01:06.548 --> 00:01:11.696
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
